---
description: Commit the plan-mode plan file to the branch so it ships with the PR.
globs: "**"
alwaysApply: true
---

When operating in plan mode:

- The plan file you write during plan mode (the `.md` file the planning tool reads before `ExitPlanMode`) MUST be committed to the current branch, not left as an uncommitted/local-only file.
- Before calling `ExitPlanMode`, stage and commit the plan file (e.g. `git add <plan-file> && git commit -m "docs: add plan for <task>"`) so it is included in the eventual Pull Request diff.
- Do not delete or gitignore the plan file after the plan is approved — it should remain in the branch history as part of the PR.
- If the plan is revised after user feedback, amend or add a follow-up commit updating the same plan file rather than leaving the update uncommitted.
